{
 "encounter_id": "00720",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello. It's the metformin. It upsets my stomach."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tell me what happens after you take it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Cramps. Then I'm running to the loo. Within an hour."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is that every time?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Most times. So I skip it sometimes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How often do you skip?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Couple of days a week. I take it twice a day, 500 mg, when I take it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So it's prescribed twice a day, but you miss it a couple of days a week. Thank you for being honest. What else do you take?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Gliclazide. 40 mg, once a day, with breakfast."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any vomiting?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Not been sick."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blood in the stool, or black stools?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blood."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any weight loss that you've noticed?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Put weight on, if anything."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your background conditions, apart from the diabetes?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Type 2 diabetes, five years. And high blood pressure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How's your diet?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Meat and veg. Lots of bread."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me press on your tummy. Lie back. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your tummy is soft and there's no tenderness."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So it's the tablets. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What you describe, cramps and loose stools within an hour of taking it, is a common side effect of metformin."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Can I stop it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please don't stop it on your own. There's a version called slow-release metformin that's much gentler on the stomach. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that different? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Same medicine, released slowly. Most people who can't tolerate the ordinary tablets manage that one. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. When do I switch? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Today. I'll sort out a new prescription, and you take it with your evening meal, never on an empty stomach."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "With food. Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Start the new one once you've finished the old tablets. Don't take both."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Understood. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the stomach trouble carries on, ring the surgery."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. Thanks. ~"
  }
 ],
